hexagon: select the chunks of the HMX 2D matmul with the cost of the kernel

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus the patches before this one in patches/series.

Files:
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/matmul-ops.h  the cost model of the kernel (htp_mm_hmx_solve_2d_cost), the chunks
                                            of a request (htp_mm_hmx_fit_2d_chunks) and their constants
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp  the switches GGML_HEXAGON_MM_SOLVER and GGML_HEXAGON_MM_CHUNKS
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp-opnode.h      the op lines of an HMX matmul give its chunks

The defect

hmx_mm_2d_f32 and hmx_mm_nx_2d_f32 have two loops. The outer loop gets m_chunk token rows and converts
their activation rows to f16 tiles one time. The inner loop moves each chunk of n_chunk weight rows
through the DMA, the dequantization and the HMX. Thus the weights go through the DMA and the
dequantization one time for each token chunk.

htp_mm_hmx_solve_2d_params adds the cost of the activation conversion for each weight chunk. Thus it
selects small token chunks, and the weights go through the DMA and the dequantization many times. At
1024 tokens of the 4B:

    ffn_down (k 9216, n 2560)               m_chunk 128, n_chunk 96, 8 passes
    ssm_out, attn_output (k 4096, n 2560)   m_chunk 384, n_chunk 192, 3 passes
    the shapes with k 2560                  2 passes

The phone stage sweep (tools/stages/sweep) measured these ops at 1024 tokens (the DSP time of a fresh op,
and the part of the op time in which the HMX operates):

    ffn_down               4165 us  51 %  thread 0 waits for the dequantization (21.9 %) and the DMA (21.2 %)
    ssm_out, attn_output   1598 us  78 %  thread 0 waits for the DMA (13.6 %)
    attn_k, attn_v          537 us  57 %
    ffn_gate, ffn_up       3069 us  92 %

The change

1. htp_mm_hmx_solve_2d_cost selects the chunks with the cost of the kernel, in ns:

       passes x n x (the DMA time + the dequantization time of one weight row)
       + passes x ceil(n / n_chunk) x HTP_MM_HMX_CHUNK_NS

   The activation conversion is the same for each selection, thus it is not a term. For each n chunk,
   the function uses the largest m chunk of the accurate layout (htp_mm_hmx_get_2d_vtcm_size). The
   estimate of htp_mm_hmx_compute_chunks adds 6 tiles, thus for ffn_down at n_chunk 32 it gives m_chunk
   320 and 4 passes. The layout of 352 rows is in the budget, and it gives 3 passes.

2. When the old selection moves the weights through the DMA one time, htp_mm_hmx_solve_2d_cost returns
   it: no selection has less passes, and the old selection has the widest n chunk. Thus an op changes its
   chunks only when the old model gives it more than one pass. At 5 to 32 tokens (the verify batch of the
   MTP draft) each op keeps its chunks. The function does not give more passes than the old model.

3. The host uses the new function for the HMX 2D kernel of MUL_MAT, MUL_MAT_ADD and MUL_MAT_NX. MUL_MAT_ID
   and the batched F16 kernel have other loops, thus they keep htp_mm_hmx_solve_2d_params. The DSP gets
   m_chunk and n_chunk in the kernel params, thus the DSP code does not change: libggml-htp-v79.so of the
   series with this patch has the bytes of the library without it.

4. GGML_HEXAGON_MM_SOLVER=0 selects the old model, for an A/B run with one library set. The preset value
   1 selects the new model. With the value 0 the backend writes the log line "ggml-hex: the HMX matmul
   chunks come from the old cost model (GGML_HEXAGON_MM_SOLVER=0)".

5. GGML_HEXAGON_MM_CHUNKS=mc,nc gives each HMX 2D matmul the chunks mc and nc when their layout is in the
   VTCM budget. A value of 0 gets the largest value for the other value. When the layout is not in the
   budget, the op keeps the chunks of the solver. The switch is for a series of chunk measurements.

6. The profile lines and the verbose op lines of an HMX matmul give "mc M nc N" after the VTCM value. The
   first word of the field stays the kernel path, thus the readers of tools/prof and tools/stages do not
   change.

The constants

    HTP_MM_HMX_DMA_BYTES_PER_US       61000  the stage sweep measured 59 to 62 GB/s for the weight stream of
                                             this kernel at 5 to 32 tokens, where the DMA sets its time
    HTP_MM_HMX_DEQUANT_PER_THREAD_US  23000  the phase trace of the stage sweep gives 18900 (k 2560) and
                                             28000 (k 9216) Q8_0 weights for each HVX thread and us
    HTP_MM_HMX_CHUNK_NS                2000  the phase trace gives less than 0.2 us for each chunk outside
                                             the phases of thread 0

At 1024 tokens, one pass of ffn_down costs 632 us in this model. The selections of the 4B shapes at 5 to
1024 tokens are the same for each chunk time from 0 to 5 us (tools/stages/mmsolve/plan.cpp sensitivity).

The chunks of the 4B at 1024 tokens (computed, tools/stages/mmsolve/plan.cpp table):

    shape                              old                      new
    ffn_down 9216x2560                 128 x 96, 8 passes       352 x 32, 3 passes
    ssm_out, attn_output 4096x2560     384 x 192, 3 passes      576 x 128, 2 passes
    ffn_gate, ffn_up 2560x9216         576 x 288, 2 passes      1024 x 128, 1 pass
    attn_qkv, attn_q 2560x8192         576 x 288, 2 passes      1024 x 128, 1 pass
    attn_gate 2560x4096                576 x 288, 2 passes      1024 x 128, 1 pass
    attn_k, attn_v 2560x1024           672 x 256, 2 passes      1024 x 128, 1 pass
    MTP ffn_down F16 9216x2560         192 x 64, 6 passes       320 x 32, 4 passes
    MTP eh_proj F16 5120x2560          288 x 128, 4 passes      544 x 64, 2 passes

The output does not change. Each output tile is one accumulator chain over all of k for each selection
of the chunks, and the conversions of the activation and of the output change each value independently.

The tests on the host

- tools/stages/mmsolve/plan.cpp check: each 4B shape (Q8_0 and the F16 MTP block) at each token count
  from 5 to 1024 (15300 cases, 5440 with other chunks) and 20000 random shapes. Each layout is in the
  budget, each chunk is a multiple of 32 in its range, the new model does not give more passes than the
  old model, and each case with one old pass keeps the old chunks. 0 failed checks.
- tests/fuzz/hexhost/run.sh test none --profile release kparams graph envparse on the tree with this
  patch: 0 findings. The graphs mode runs the real graphs of the 2B and the 4B (decode, prefill 512, the
  MTP draft and its verify batch, the image turn) against the checks of the DSP layout of each op.
- tools/htp-lab target mmchunks (the functional simulator, the lab flags and the release flags): MUL_MAT,
  MUL_MAT with src2 and MUL_MAT_NX of Q8_0 and F16 weights, 31 runs of 7 cases with the old chunks, the
  new chunks and requests down to n_chunk 32. Each run gives the bytes of the run with the old chunks.

